{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/343100-mark-of-the-beast-confusion","id":343100,"title":"Mark of the Beast Confusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-17T10:56:58-08:00","id":343100,"title":"Mark of the Beast Confusion","content":"Okay, so there's a little confusion given the wording of the fluff, then the mechanics of this Castigation. The fluff states the following.; &quot;One member might take the form of a fallen angel with ripped and tattered wings, weeping tears of blood that mar otherwise perfect features, while the form of another member might echo the bestial nature of her sire complete with burning red eyes, claws, and fangs. The demonic visage remains consistent each time the hunter activates the Castigation, leading some of the Lucifuge to wonder if the demonic version isn\u2019t their soul\u2019s \u201ctrue\u201d form.&quot;<br /> <br /> But the confusion comes from the mechanics; &quot;While transformed, the hunter gains a pool of points equal to her Castigation score that she may use to increase any Physical Attribute in any combination she desires.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, does this mean the Hunter can allocate dots however they desire each time the Castigation is activated? Or is that wording purely for the purpose of explaining how to allocate dots as you raise Castigation, and the stats are locked each time you activate it?<br /> <br /> Any light that could be shed on it would be appreciated, preferably from a developer, as I know players tend to have different opinions when it comes to the letter of rules.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T04:40:39-08:00","id":343779,"title":"","content":"Since the shape is consistent, I'd go with choose once and then it's locked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T22:28:39-08:00","id":346474,"title":"","content":"The thing is, nothing in the mechanics whatsoever says that the stats are locked. Quite the opposite, in fact. The part about the &quot;demonic visage&quot; remaining consistent is exactly that, to me. i.e, the demonic visage and nothing more, meaning that the demon doesn't one day look like Hellboy, and the next time he shifts looks like Cthulhu. Just seems more to me like an aesthetic restriction, rather than mechanical.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the mechanics, again, say exactly as I copy pasted above, with no indication that they cannot be spread around in whatever combination each time the Hunter uses the Castigation. It's basically a rather common sense mechanic which is thrown into the realms of obscurity by a single line of text in the fluff half of the power.<br /> <br /> Again, players and STs are going to differ on their opinions in this, so if the developers which wrote the Castigation, or - if they are no longer Onyx Path employees - a developer who at least knows the intent could give their opinion on the matter, it would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}